In your view, you check `request.method` and bind the form to the POST data.

```python
def contact(request):
    if request.method == 'POST':
        form = ContactForm(request.POST)
        if form.is_valid():
            # Process the data
            name = form.cleaned_data['name']
            # ...
            return redirect('success')
    else:
        form = ContactForm()
    return render(request, 'contact.html', {'form': form})
```

- `is_valid()` runs validation and returns `True` if all fields pass.
- `cleaned_data` contains the validated data (type‑converted).

Errors are automatically available in `form.errors`. In the template, you can show them:

```html
{% if form.errors %}
    <div class="errors">
        <p>Please correct the errors below:</p>
        {{ form.non_field_errors }}
    </div>
{% endif %}

{% for field in form %}
    {{ field.errors }}
    {{ field.label_tag }}
    {{ field }}
{% endfor %}
```
